      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LOCHINVAR JAG (7) has won three straight and arrives here full of confidence after taking control well before the finish to score at Penrith. This is a step up, but he is racing too well to dismiss and another victory is certainly within reach. PARTY CENTRAL NZ (1) failed to fire when fifth here last start, but his form prior was much stronger, including a win over this trip two starts ago. The pole draw should allow him to get an economical run and he can bounce back. MAGIC JOE (6) wasn't disgraced when fourth over 2300m here and has the ability to be competitive if he gets the right tempo. LETS TURN IT ON (5) is capable on his day, and with some luck from a handy gate, he can figure in the top 4 at a decent price. OUR SUNSET DELIGHT (10) comes into calculations after another honest fourth at Albion Park and if he gets a start of the ballot, then he can figure in the finish with the right run.",
